{"id": "xturkey", "name": "Kaçkar Mountains National Park", "short": "Kaçkar Mountains", "place": "Turkey", "lat": 40.83, "lon": 41.15, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Turkey", "blurb": "Glaciated peaks, chamois and bears above the Black Sea forests.", "tip": {"id": "wolf", "title": "Remove the wolves", "text": "Wolves, lynx and bears all hunt chamois and roe deer. Set Gray wolf to -100% and watch the deer and chamois, then the meadow plants they graze."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Kaçkar Mountains", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaçkar_Mountains"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Caucasian grouse", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caucasian_grouse"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Chamois", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamois"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Brown bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_bear"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Kaçkar Mountains", "icon": "ice", "tier": "overview", "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "nodes": [{"id": "rhodo", "sp": "rhododendron caucasicum", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "grass", "sp": "poa", "xh": 0.28, "name": "Alpine meadow grasses", "wiki": "Poaceae", "desc": "Highland grasses and herbs that cover the meadows above the tree line in summer and feed grazers such as chamois.", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "gentian", "sp": "gentiana septemfida", "xh": 0.46}, {"id": "spruce", "sp": "picea orientalis", "xh": 0.64}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus orientalis", "xh": 0.82, "desc": "A broadleaf forest tree of the Black Sea slopes whose nuts are food for dormice, squirrels and wild boar.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "chamois", "sp": "rupicapra rupicapra", "xh": 0.04, "desc": "Eats highland grasses and herbs in summer and conifer needles and bark in winter. The Anatolian subspecies lives in Turkey.", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.17, "desc": "A small forest deer and prey for the region's lynx, wolves and bears."}, {"id": "goat", "sp": "capra hircus", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Goats graze the mountain slopes and are reported living wild in the range. Large carnivores take them."}, {"id": "grouse", "sp": "lyrurus mlokosiewiczi", "xh": 0.43}, {"id": "squirrel", "sp": "sciurus anomalus", "xh": 0.56}, {"id": "dormouse", "sp": "glis glis", "xh": 0.69, "wiki": "Edible dormouse", "desc": "A nocturnal tree-climbing rodent that eats nuts, seeds and fruit, and is hunted by foxes and lynx.", "ic": "vole"}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.82, "desc": "An omnivore of the forests, rooting for nuts, roots and small animals, and listed among the range's large mammals."}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Red fox", "desc": "A generalist hunter of small mammals and birds that also takes carrion."}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.5, "wiki": "Common raven", "desc": "A scavenger that feeds on carcasses of mountain ungulates, often alongside larger carnivores."}, {"id": "vulture", "sp": "gypaetus barbatus", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "A mountain vulture recorded near the park that feeds mainly on the bones and remains of dead animals."}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "ursus arctos", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "An omnivore taking most of its energy from plants but also hunting and scavenging; the Eastern Black Sea region holds Turkey's bears.", "badge": "Ecosystem engineer"}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.5, "wiki": "Wolf", "desc": "Pack hunter listed among the range's large mammals and a historic predator of chamois."}, {"id": "lynx", "sp": "lynx lynx", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "A solitary cat that preys on chamois, roe deer and smaller animals in forest and rocky terrain.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "summer sun", "xh": 0.08}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "snowpack & 